	(text "ADC345_IN11"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 618.236 240.284 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "0c803a2d-a02b-40db-ade3-70e83a43bf47")
	)
	(text "PWM_Enable:\n\nThe PWM_Enable net controls when the PWM Fiber Gate Driver ICs\ndrive the PWM fiber transmitters. If at any time PWM_Enable is\npulled LOW (0V), all IX4340NTR outputs will immediately be driven\nto 0V and the versatile link transmitters stop transmitting a\nfiber optic signal.\n\nAll 12 FET board Gate Drivers transmit a fiber optic \"OK\" signal\nto the HVPS V3 board. A jumper J14 allows selection between\nnormally LOW Gate Driver \"OK\" signal and normally HIGH Gate Driver\n\"OK\" signal. Typical operation will have Normally_High_GD_Enable\nand GDS_Enable nets tied together.\n\nAs a sign of good faith to those less trustworthy of microcontrollers,\nthe AND gate U54D has been allocated to compute \nGDS_Enable AND Fiber_Enable. This allows remote disabling of the PWM\noutput. In the event this functionality is not required, R67 may be\npopulated to pull Fiber_Enable to +5V (HIGH).\n\nFinally, the net STM_Enable exists for more precise control of the \nPWM output timing. If PWM outputs are clean enough so as to not \nrequire a rolling output selection, for instance clipping the \nbeginning period or terminating period of a PWM output, the\ncorresponding pin on the STM32G4 microcontroller should be set\nHIGH by default, and remain always on."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at -369.57 769.62 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.54 2.54)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "0cb8cc5a-b2bd-416d-9a81-795d1b9ed5b1")
	)
